{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-29T21:41:34.849Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/watcher/build.ts` (now 229 lines, under 250): added `STALE_BUILD_MESSAGE`, `StaleBuildError`, `FindStaleBuildOptions`, `findStaleBuild` (returns the line or `null`, accepts optional `distMtimeMs`), `newestDistMtimeMs`, and `osqPackageRoot`. `checkStaleBuild` is now a thin print-and-exit wrapper over `findStaleBuild`.\n- New `src/watcher/stale-pass.ts` (61 lines): `StaleCheck`, `assertNotStale`, `startStaleCheck` (start check + cached `dist/` mtime), and `handleStaleBuild`.\n- `src/watcher/loop.ts`: optional fifth `StaleCheck` arg on `runWatcherCycle`/`runWatcherOnce`; `StaleBuildError` thrown at the top of the pending-task branch and of `archiveCompletedSpec`; per-change catch rethrows it; `startWatcher` builds the check from `findStaleBuild`, adds `packageRoot`/`exit` options, and stops/clears/prints/exits(1) on a stale build (start check, `once` mode, and `cycleHandler`).\n- `tests/watcher-stale-every-pass.test.ts`: four scenarios (source edited during a run, allow-stale during a run, stale before first spawn, rebuilt without restart).\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify: 9 tests pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: typechecks, build, full test suite, and lint all pass.\n\n**Documented deviation** (in the result file): the task/spec say `.run/done/1.md`, but the watcher has always written `.run/done/1`; the test asserts the real path and no marker-naming code was touched.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/118-stale-build-every-pass/.run/results/1.md`.\n\nTouched: src/watcher/build.ts, src/watcher/loop.ts, src/watcher/stale-pass.ts, tests/watcher-stale-every-pass.test.ts"}}
